From 791ad570b1285f1e8e1326076448fcf599ae2261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:39:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Distillation: STOP-factorised KL, reachability gate,
 counterfactual map-effect matching

The plain action-level KL asks the LLM-map student to match the GT-map
teacher's whole action distribution, most of which depends on the GT route
corridor the student cannot see. Three opt-in terms separate the part that
can be transferred (all default to the historical plain KL):

- IL.distill_stop_factorized: KL = stop_weight * KL(Bernoulli STOP)
  + KL(move | not STOP), so the stop decision can be weighted separately.
- IL.gate_enabled: per-step weight min + (1 - min) * exp(-JS / tau), with JS
  between the teacher on its GT map and the teacher on the student's LLM map
  (same legacy format). Steps where the LLM map misleads the teacher itself
  are down-weighted, never dropped. tau <= 0 uses the batch median JS.
- IL.effect_match_weight: squared error between the student's and the
  teacher's map effect on the (valid-set centred) logits, each measured
  against a counterfactual map (own metadata, raster from another episode of
  the batch via a scene-mismatch-maximising derangement, or zeros). Vision
  and language cancel in the difference, so the student can only lower it
  through its map pathway; the teacher side and the student counterfactual
  branch are detached.

Counterfactual and gate map tokens are encoded once per rollout (maps are
static; refiner and map ablations are rejected). Logs: effect_loss,
gate_mean, teacher_llm_ce, stop_kl, move_kl.

scripts/distill/run_dagger_distill_legacy.sh {kl|gated|full}: GT-legacy
18600 teacher (dy, legacy r1.5 m GT map) into an isomorphic LLM-Grid try5
student (460000 backbone, map modules from initialisation, no coordinate
fusion). kl is the historical control arm.

Unit tests (tests/etp_prior_gt/test_distill_losses.py, 15): masked softmax,
KL equals the historical formula, chain-rule identity of the factorisation,
effect matching zero up to a constant and invariant to shared shifts with
gradient only through the student's own-map branch, JS range, gate floor and
median scale, donor permutation.

